  "identifier": "qupath",
  "name": "QuPath",
  "description": "The leading open-source platform for digital pathology and bioimage analysis — used in virtually every computational pathology lab worldwide. Supports whole-slide image annotation, cell detection and segmentation, tissue microarray analysis, fluorescence and brightfield analysis, interactive machine learning for tissue classification, and scripting via Groovy for batch workflows. Integrates with StarDist, OMERO, and ImageJ. Java-based, cross-platform (Windows, macOS, Linux). Developed at the University of Edinburgh by Pete Bankhead, funded by Wellcome Trust and Chan Zuckerberg Initiative. GPL-3.0, 1.4k stars, 342 forks, v0.7.0 (March 2026).",
